<section class="panel rules-page"><h1>Rules of the First Realm</h1><p>Kingdom Come is a multiplayer alpha inspired by Kingdoms Live. Our catalog and numerical rules are reconstructed, not recovered original server formulas.</p><h2>Quest, equip, invest</h2><p>Explore eleven regions with quests and equipment through level 50, then work toward the Worldroot Bastion at level 55. Mana runs repeatable quests. Equipment requirements stay owned; discoveries open later routes. Each army member automatically uses at most one weapon, one armor item and one spell; attack and defense choose different best items. Sales refund half the recorded paid cost per copy, rounded down.</p><h2>Resources and skills</h2><p>Health starts at 100, Mana at 20 and Spirit at 3. Recover 10 Health every 3 minutes, 1 Mana every 5 minutes and 1 Spirit every 2 minutes. Level-ups restore resources. One skill point adds 1 Mana or 10 Health; two add 1 Spirit. One point buys one Attack or Defense rating: +1% to the relevant army power, capped at 25 ratings each. Existing allocations remain unchanged. These training rules are reconstructed. Level milestones, ten quests and your first attacking victory award additional points.</p><h2>Land and upkeep</h2><p>Property pays every full 60 minutes after purchase, including offline hours. Each additional property of the same type costs 10% more. Existing holdings keep their saved rates. All owned upkeep equipment accrues maintenance while funded. A reserve and carried gold pay it after due Land income; no passive income is required to buy equipment.</p><p>If funds run out, upkeep equipment pauses, free gear remains usable and further charges stop. Arrears never exceed one hourly bill at suspension. Resume pays arrears and reserves one hour. No equipment is destroyed. Selling gear returns reserve above the new hourly bill; recorded arrears remain. The gold header shows Land income minus property upkeep and currently active equipment upkeep; paused gear is excluded.</p><h2>Rivals</h2><p>Attack uses 1 Spirit and requires both warriors to have 20 Health. Similar-level rivals are eligible; a short cooldown applies. Gold moves between players, with capped loot. At most three initiated encounters per rival in 24 hours can award gold/XP.</p><h2>Your army</h2><p>You, accepted allies and retained militia share an active army limit that grows with level. Excess recruits stay owned. Each leader equips their own force. Callings are cosmetic identities during alpha.</p><p>Active ruleset: <strong><%= alpha.id %></strong>. Resources, purchases, sales, combat and payments are decided by the server.</p><a class="button button-outline" href="<%= state?'/game/home':'/login' %>">Return to realm</a></section>
